  "_zoneNotes": [
    "Every zone carries a `surface` and, for anything that rests on something,",
    "a `base`: the art y of the CONTACT LINE it stands on, read off the room",
    "plate at full size. An object is drawn so its foot lands on `base`, which is",
    "what makes a 150 px pen and a 240 px van both sit on the same shelf edge.",
    "`surface: wall` has no base — it hangs, and gets a cast shadow instead of a",
    "contact ellipse. x/y/w/h stay the allowed box: x still centres and clamps,",
    "y is only used when there is no base.",
    "Phase 3 re-tuned every rect against the plates; the §4.3 table in",
    "game-design.md is the older, un-grounded lattice.",
    "",
    "NO ZONE MAY INTERSECT THE TARGET SPRITE'S BOX. The target is pinned at",
    "tuning.targetSpriteArt and is 340 art px tall, so it owns roughly art",
    "(630..970, 410..760) after the HUD reserve lifts it clear of the word card.",
    "The kitchen and bedroom both used to put a sill zone straight through it —",
    "case 3's hen stood on the ladybug's back and case 5's net crossed the jet's",
    "nose. Both are now `window-front`: a wall hang over the upper glass, above",
    "the target and below the prompt banner. If a zone is ever re-tuned, the QC",
    "screenshot pass has to re-check every case that uses it, in both modes —",
    "sound-detective shuffles all five objects across all eight zones, so a bad",
    "zone is a bug in five cases, not in the one that happens to name it."
  ],

