  "_footPadNotes": [
    "hotspot-scene.js draws every sprite inside a SQUARE art box (wideBox's",
    "`s x s`) with CSS object-fit:contain, centred on both axes. A sprite whose",
    "raster aspect is wider than it is tall (a flat mat, a squat fruit) is",
    "width-constrained inside that square, which leaves vertical slack split",
    "evenly above and below — so its drawn foot lands `slack/2` art px ABOVE the",
    "zone's grounding `base` line instead of on it, i.e. it visibly floats.",
    "`footPad[word]` is that half-slack in art px, computed once from the",
    "shipped sprite's own pixel aspect at its configured `sizes[word]`:",
    "  slackHalf = (s - s * (imgH / imgW)) / 2   -- only when imgW > imgH",
    "wideBox adds it to the grounded y so the RASTER's foot (not the box's)",
    "sits on `base`. Only zones with a `base` (floor/shelf) are affected; wall",
    "zones centre the sprite regardless, so a word only needs an entry here if",
    "some case actually places it in a grounded zone. Re-measure and update",
    "this map whenever mat.webp or fig.webp (or any future flat/wide sprite) is",
    "regenerated at a different aspect ratio."
  ],
  "footPad": {
    "mat": 47,
    "fig": 18
  },

